Minor spoilers...

So here I am on the castle level, deciding that I would make things easier by
filling in the first two or three trapdoors in the line with boulders, since
I would probably be making a couple of trips across them.  I manage to use a
wand of digging to eliminate enough wall to maneuver one boulder around, but
the others are hopelessly wedged in corners of the screen; so I decide to use
my rings of polymorph and polymorph control to change into a giant and carry
the boulders over.

All goes well, I am now a frost giant carrying a boulder over to the next
trapdoor.  But instead of dropping and pushing it, I decide to just walk over
the trapdoor and drop the boulder in it (this is what I assume will happen).
Instead, as soon as I walk onto the trapdoor, I fall through it *with the
boulder still in my hands!*  So if I push the boulder, it will wedge itself
in the trapdoor, but if I carry it, it will fit through :-).  

Actually, I don't think giants should be able to fall through trapdoors, or 
if they can, then when they do something like I did, maybe they should get
helplessly wedged in them with the boulder.  Creativity could abound on this
one....
